# Rank 1616 / CVE-2023-0299: Publify's core models declared string
# attributes whose length only MySQL's implicit 255-character column
# limit bounded -- on other databases the values persisted unbounded
# and broke deployments relying on the implicit cap (missing
# cross-database input bounds, CWE-20/CWE-400; the sweep fixing all
# string attributes at once). The models under publify_core/app/
# models carried no length validations for string columns. Pool
# commit 34f6e9c98e is the fixing change,"Validate lengths
# of string attributes", 18 models): a shared
# validates_default_string_length(*names) concern applies
# `validates name, length: { maximum: STRING_LIMIT }` (255) to every
# string attribute -- titles, authors, permalinks, emails, urls,
# mime types, redirect paths -- plus an explicit 40 for ip. No pool
# correction (the task list's repo! flag mirrors rank 1615's: the
# advisory names publify/publify while this commit lives in
# publify/publify_core; the pool row's repository is the one holding
# the fixing change).
#
# ATTENTION, cross-database attribute budgets. The same family as
# rank 1615 (the name-length fix eleven minutes earlier in the
# sibling repo), generalised: the implicit database limit is not a
# validation, and no rule can ask "does every string attribute
# enforce the limit its schema assumes" -- model-validation
# vocabulary across schema dialects. A binding on Publify's own
# concern would detect this application rather than the weakness.
# Measured on the real code: scanning app/models/user.rb reports
# zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1616 records the
# unvalidated string attributes and the shared-limit form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-DOS-029: when attribute-budget vocabulary
# lands, the unvalidated form must flip to expect.

test "rank1616: string attributes carry no length validation"
  lang ruby
  file publify_core/app/models/user.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class User < ActiveRecord::Base
    validates :email, presence: true, uniqueness: true
    validates :login, presence: true, uniqueness: true
    validates :name, presence: true

    def permalink_url(anchor)
      "#{blog.base_url}authors/#{login}##{anchor}"
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1616: the fixed revision applies the default string limit"
  lang ruby
  file publify_core/app/models/user.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class User < ActiveRecord::Base
    include Validations::DefaultStringLimits

    validates :email, presence: true, uniqueness: true
    validates :login, presence: true, uniqueness: true
    validates :name, presence: true

    validates_default_string_length :email, :login, :name, :display_name,
                                    :permalink, :filter, :state

    def permalink_url(anchor)
      "#{blog.base_url}authors/#{login}##{anchor}"
    end
  end

  module Validations
    module DefaultStringLimits
      extend ActiveSupport::Concern

      STRING_LIMIT = 255

      class_methods do
        def validates_default_string_length(*names)
          names.each do |name|
            validates name, length: { maximum: STRING_LIMIT }
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
